{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends","id":1520386,"title":"So, Crucible of Legends","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-11T08:00:41-07:00","id":1520386,"title":"So, Crucible of Legends","content":"What are your thoughts?<br /> <br /> Is it worthy?<br /> <br /> Can it improve the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T15:17:33-07:00","id":1520414,"title":"","content":"I guess it depends what you wanted out of it?<br /> <br /> As the storytelling chapter that the core book never got? It's good. It's very nicely cohesive, so when it talks about different modes of playing the game, and then moves on to other topics, it makes sure to relate how different things work with or against the different modes and how to deal with that.<br /> <br /> The optional rules are solid, but they're not as extensive as I think a lot of us were hoping to see. Actually having things for Bureaucracy to do is nice and I think helps edge Bureaucracy and Crafts closer, so when characters want to build things that require teams to construct, there's more for leaders and logistics types to actually add instead of such things either being some sort of small bonus for a main crafter, or the core's hand wave it approach. The Craft fixes are fine, but I doubt are going to completely satisfy people that don't like 3e's base crafting premise; but it is easier to make someone that isn't a craft-machine and still does craft stuff on the side. The Naval Combat fixes are probably not a lot of people's first concern, but it definitely addressed the issues people had with the system in a way that should make naval fights a lot more appealing for group play.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure entirely how I feel about the new stuff with Virtues (even if those were largely lifted from Essence) and Limit. Some tweaks to Stunts was unexpected and I'm still contemplating how I feel about them.<br /> <br /> I was disappointed that we didn't get a much more simplified QC system. The book doesn't do anything bad here, I just wanted to see them go farther. Running large fights with multiple Exalted NPCs is still going to be daunting if you want it to While I'm glad they didn't just spend a 1/4 of the book on combat, the complexity of managing NPCs is by far the biggest issue I hear from people that are nervous about running the game. I'm not sure this is going to get someone sitting on the fence off it. For those of us that are older hands at the game, the fixes to the other stuff are going to feel more impactful because we've already factored in Exalted resource tracking in combat as just a part of the game. For people that have the core book and are scared of running a fight where some Wyld Hunt Dragonbloods attack the PCs in a big action set piece? I'm not sure this is going to help them enough.<br /> <br /> So... would I recommend it? Sure. There's nothing that struck me as bad, and a lot of good, even if it's not prioritized on things I might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T17:49:52-07:00","id":1520419,"title":"","content":"My Feedback/Review on CoL:-<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Errata Needed:-</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Opening fiction: Is Wandering Teeth meant to be a Solar or Infernal? He is described as both.<br /> Lots of sections with XX instead of page numbers.</div> <br /> <br /> <b>Disappointment:-</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Nothing about a System for Occult. Was not really expecting it but hope springs eternal.<br /> <br /> Orientalism section is not that useful as in I can't understand why it was there?<br /> <br /> Would have liked to see something on how throw off the 'magical' detection ability of (Sidereal) Wyld Hunt. - I can hand wave it as an ST but as a player I would like to know what steps I can take to counter it specifically.<br /> <br /> The alternate settings were nice but heavily focused on removing different exalts. I would have liked other changes like increasing/decreasing the level of magic to be considered.</div> <br /> <br /> <b>Wait and See:-</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Craft System seems decent. I am not full savvy at Mechanics so will wait and what the more dedicated fans make of it. In all honesty I have slowly gotten to like the base core craft system, it's the Solar charms that need...work.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Mandate of Heaven : Better then the nothing that was there previously. Again need to see what fans make of it and how it comes up in actual play. I did want more focus on how the bureaucracy ability is used with this system.</div><div style=\"margin-left:80px\">Layout Issue: I would have preferred the actual mandate rules first and then 'lite' rules that hook onto the Core system second.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Virtues : I consider them interesting, not sure with the seven specified but adding/removing is easy but I do have a question:- Are the 2E virtues still on the table? The initial text implies they have been replaced but later it mentions Conviction. Not sure if this is on purpose or error.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Unified Experience Point Costs : Again a wait and see. I am a bit surprised at the lower merit &amp; willpower cost as well as the increased charm, evocation &amp; spell costs.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Good:-</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Section on Styles of Play was excellent.<br /> The reminder on 'Spending Willpower to resist Social Influence' Facts being introduced by any ability now.<br /> Great Curse Section is great.<br /> Legendary Social Goals explained and Expanded.<br /> The &quot;How Fast Do I Go&quot; Sidebar was needed.</div> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T09:19:15-07:00","id":1520456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1520419#post1520419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Errata Needed:-</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Lots of sections with XX instead of page numbers.</div>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was standard for OPP's pre-errata phase? They sub in page numbers once the feedback and correction phase completes, unless I've misunderstood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T10:08:35-07:00","id":1520459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1520456#post1520456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that was standard for OPP's pre-errata phase? They sub in page numbers once the feedback and correction phase completes, unless I've misunderstood.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, they mentioned when it dropped that this is in the early phase and for any proofing or corrections to ignore the XX page numbers as they're aware of those and will fix them once its ready for final drop. My guess is its partially to mark it as unfinished and partially in case something comes up that potentially alters book placement like how the core forgot to include a stat block for a creature in backer drop or how in one of my class projects a formatting glitch caused a page to mirror its own text on the other side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T22:31:46-07:00","id":1520501,"title":"","content":"One thing I really liked was the Unified XP system, especially having players gain 10 XP every session. What that means is that now, players can buy 1 new charm after every session. Let me tell you, players having a new shiny thing every time they play can really help retain enthusiasm for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T12:00:53-07:00","id":1520693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1520419#post1520419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orientalism section is not that useful as in I can't understand why it was there?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> Mind unpacking this?<br /> <br /> For my part, my issue with that section is that while I agree with what it\u2019s saying it feels like it\u2019s directed more at people who want to publish Exalted content than the collaborative efforts of a storyteller and their players. I'd have certainly opened with why indulging orientalism isn't good for people's game groups even if there's no asian people at the table to take offense to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T13:39:08-07:00","id":1520703,"title":"","content":"The issue with the Orientalism essay that I seen and kind of agree with is that it is not in itself bad to have, but needed to present itself in a more <i>actionable</i> manner. That is to say, pointing out the issue and saying some more on what to do about it for one's games would have made it feel a bit more complete.<br /> <br /> This is an issue also found with the QC advice, which could have had some more actual numbers rather than the obvious &quot;If soak is too high lower it&quot; stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T15:25:07-07:00","id":1520717,"title":"","content":"I think the Orientalism piece is a bit of an impossible needle to thread. While what amounts to an extended disclaimer of &quot;We know Exalted is guilty of plenty of Orientalism, but it's bad and we should all aim to not do it,&quot; isn't terribly actionable... there's not a lot of actionable you can do with such a limited amount of space. And I would argue there's at least some actionable stuff in there like pointing out that if you're playing in English, use English words over trying to &quot;spice up&quot; your language with borrow words as you're not borrowing from Low Realm if you borrow from Thai to make your English language play sound more special.<br /> <br /> If the section was 10 pages, they could have done a lot more actionable material in it, sure, but there's a diminishing return: the more people care about not doing Orientalism, the less they need a 10 page essay about it in a RPG supplement, and people that care less about such things aren't going to have the patience to read through 10 pages of stuff they're not sold on the base premise of. People write full scholarly books about these topics.. there's a point where a section in a ST supplement for Exalted has to just point out that this is a thing, and trust people that care to put in work for themselves to go farther if they feel called to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T19:27:34-07:00","id":1520733,"title":"","content":"Honestly, some suggested readings for sections like that I think would have also honestly not been a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T08:54:57-07:00","id":1521257,"title":"","content":"It's too soon to say how I feel about the Mandate of Rulership but I'm very interested in the Risk Tracker and if that can address the core issue I've observed with previous attempts at leadership systems where they heavily associate complications and consequences stemming from the leadership action with failed dice rolls. I like that it seems to offer an element of unpredictability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T15:16:26-07:00","id":1521408,"title":"","content":"I hoped for very little.<br /> I got very little. This book does a lot of little fixes that were needed. The ideas for alternative resolution Initiative was pretty cool.<br /> While I do not understand why we did not just port Ventures, Mandate of Rulership and the rest of <br /> <br /> But, it could not save Exalted from the Sail System. Nor the immense Craft section.<br /> <br /> I *wanted* Essence Qualities, yet got a vague guideline for QCs.<br /> <br /> The entire Orientalism chapter is not really actionable, and would probably have required an entire book in itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtues</b>. I want them out of exalted so much that it feels like there's a buzzsaw in my bones.<br /> <br /> Basically. It's a mixed bag, but it has a lot of heart.<br /> <br /> Yet. It suffers from a strange cross-contamination - it reads like a lot of other OPP books and not like an Exalted book. That is not an entirely positive thing.<br /> While it might cut down on the amount of freelancers only needed in the Exalted silo, something about the book makes a lot of the same wishy-washy statements that I've found all across Scion and Trinity and a few other Storypath products.<br /> <br /> Sigh. I must honestly have hoped for something more, in spite of what I am saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T23:02:13-07:00","id":1521418,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out that my extended family and friends thinks the obessession with not offending people because of oreientelism is stupid. Use the words if you want. Call the guy that trains your character sensei (it means the guy who teaches you as a Honorific, hell thats how they use it in Japan). It doesn't matter, use words and things from all across the world if it helps your game feel cooler. The people over there do not care, and in fact want you too. It's wierdos that heard stupid stuff on American Websites or American Universities or on terrible youtube videos care about. How do I know this, my wife and friends are from those countries and they ask me sometimes what the heck is going on. <br /> seriously the people who live in all the counties of Asia do not care that you use those terms. They want you to use them, to learn about those words, countries and cultures. So then you start consuming thier media. Watch more anime, watch more Wushu films (back in the day they were called Kung Fu films) Watch K-Dramas, call your crush opa (Korean for brother) [ I tell my wife not to it's wierd].<br /> <br /> Be a dork, weeb out, and be awesome to one another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T04:08:26-07:00","id":1521423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1521418#post1521418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The people over there do not care, and in fact want you too. It's wierdos that heard stupid stuff on American Websites or American Universities or on terrible youtube videos care about. How do I know this, my wife and friends are from those countries and they ask me sometimes what the heck is going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mainly the diaspora, many of whom have experienced racism based on this relatively small window into asian cultures who'll be uncomfortable and they're likely to be a significant part of the asian people that the English speaking audience of the book will interact with, let alone play Exalted with.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T10:41:53-07:00","id":1521435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1521423#post1521423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mainly the diaspora, many of whom have experienced racism based on this relatively small window into asian cultures who'll be uncomfortable and they're likely to be a significant part of the asian people that the English speaking audience of the book will interact with, let alone play Exalted with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would have preferred if the section on orientalism brought that up and took the approach that it's a good idea to communicate with your players to find out how these concepts can be presented in a way that everyone enjoys in-game.<br /> <br /> Instead it came across to me with a very different attitude, literally saying &quot;don't do this&quot; about some things which are arguably core to the game. I found it bizarre that in the intro sub-section, it says that we, the players, have to &quot;counteract&quot; the &quot;strong orientalist traditions&quot; in the Exalted game, or that it is a &quot;Western misconception&quot; that Asian fighting styles are &quot;more esoteric, mystical&quot;, and presents that as if it is an insult. I am willing to assume that may be a valid concern for some real-world martial arts, but at least in the realm of the fantastic wuxia-inspired martial arts that are the inspiration for Exalted content, I don't think using the terms esoteric or mystical are invalid or insulting. And I feel fairly confident that most of the audience of this book, ie people who have enough investment in Exalted to be buying this book, probably don't feel that wuxia-inspired martial arts are a negative aspect that we have to downplay in our private home games in order to be respectful citizens of the world.<br /> <br /> That may not be the intent of the author, but I can only speak to how it came across to me. That section, and some areas of chapter one, felt like they strayed out of the realm of game content and into something else.<br /> <br /> Note: Edited the first sentence to more coherently respond to the quoted section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","user":"Lindharin","date":". 08-26-2023, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T11:51:14-07:00","id":1521437,"title":"","content":"Let's be honest if you watch Pili a Taiwanese puppet show, it just drips with all the stuff that people say would be problematic if I tried it. But what I am being told is to actually really care about is if my dad happens to get up set if some southern boy puts ketchup on his meatballs and calls it spaghetti.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T18:05:46-07:00","id":1521450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindharin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1521435#post1521435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have preferred if the section on orientalism brought that up and took the approach that it's a good idea to communicate with your players to find out how these concepts can be presented in a way that everyone enjoys in-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be my preference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindharin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead it came across to me with a very different attitude, literally saying &quot;don't do this&quot; about some things which are arguably core to the game. I found it bizarre that in the intro sub-section, it says that we, the players, have to &quot;counteract&quot; the &quot;strong orientalist traditions&quot; in the Exalted game, or that it is a &quot;Western misconception&quot; that Asian fighting styles are &quot;more esoteric, mystical&quot;, and presents that as if it is an insult. I am willing to assume that may be a valid concern for some real-world martial arts, but at least in the realm of the fantastic wuxia-inspired martial arts that are the inspiration for Exalted content, I don't think using the terms esoteric or mystical are invalid or insulting. And I feel fairly confident that most of the audience of this book, ie people who have enough investment in Exalted to be buying this book, probably don't feel that wuxia-inspired martial arts are a negative aspect that we have to downplay in our private home games in order to be respectful citizens of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree on any particular point.<br /> I'm not sure that's what the Martial Arts section is actually getting at but the fact I'm not sure and you (and others) have that interpretation of it is a problem.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T03:02:17-07:00","id":1521498,"title":"","content":"Anyway, what I think the Martial Arts section is saying.<br /> <br /> I think that it's calling out the initial decision back in 1st edition to split unarmed combat into Brawl and Martial Arts (because there's a lot of pre-existing baggage there) and wants us to critically examine when we're picking one of those abilities over the other. There's brawlers who learned to fight in a formal school and self-taught martial artists. <br /> <br /> IMO that's healthier than what I've seen in some circles where brawl's established a semblance of identity for itself through the rejection of wuxia tropes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T08:04:43-07:00","id":1521510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1521498#post1521498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, what I think the Martial Arts section is saying.<br /> <br /> I think that it's calling out the initial decision back in 1st edition to split unarmed combat into Brawl and Martial Arts (because there's a lot of pre-existing baggage there) and wants us to critically examine when we're picking one of those abilities over the other. There's brawlers who learned to fight in a formal school and self-taught martial artists.<br /> <br /> IMO that's healthier than what I've seen in some circles where brawl's established a semblance of identity for itself through the rejection of wuxia tropes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's even a bit of a call-out of 3e, where the split was brought back. Then MAs went on to be Fancy Brawl versus Brawl-is-an-Abilty-but-not-Skill shit htat I remember actually confusing folks on the forums when it was brought-up. We couldn't get a straight answer as to whether Jeet Kun Doh was Brawl or not, and apparently the view of the devs then was &quot;No&quot; as that was skill and Brawl 5 was apparently just Good Punching WIthout Training. WHich did kind of push the Orientalist bent in things there uncomfortably.<br /> <br /> Like, at a point Martial Arts worked more like Essence, where you had Archery and Melee Styles, which I think was a good route. But hten &quot;Brawl Style&quot; was seen as contradictory for...reasons. It kind of is somewhat I think the text pointing out htis was probably a bad decision from even just the try-not-to-be-Orientalist take, just dind't artiuclate it best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T13:10:55-07:00","id":1521527,"title":"","content":"Well, the problem is also that charm empowered brawl particularly for Solar Exalted is a little too good in an end the fight by throwing a single punch kind of way and well, that\u2019s similar to how some people perceive the East vs. West divide where Asia has a lot of style and pageantry that\u2019s no match for brutal efficiency. <br /> <br /> There's something extremely macho about being <b>so strong</b> that it doesn't matter if the other person is more skilled than you and as I say this I realise that I'm struggling to think of a brawler (or hero stylist) among the named characters of 3 editions who was actually coded as Asian. I think possibly White Bone Sinner? Maybe!?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-28-2023, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T14:05:25-07:00","id":1521531,"title":"","content":"<s>Wind, maybe? He <i>is</i> basically a shaolin monk. Same with Deled.</s> misread, forgot the &quot;brawler&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T02:30:32-07:00","id":1521962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1521408#post1521408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Virtues</b>. I want them out of exalted so much that it feels like there's a buzzsaw in my bones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. What I find interesting about the implementation of Virtues both here and in Essence is that there is no framework for channeling your virtue into your action which was, at least in my opinion, the actually <i>fun</i> part of playing a virtuous character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T13:03:25-07:00","id":1522004,"title":"","content":"Losing my mind that we finally have a Storyteller's Guide <i>and it doesn't have any guidance for handling Merits in play.</i><br /> <br /> On my knees begging for someone, anyone, to descend from their lofty eminence and explain the nuances of Influence and Resources and Backing and all the ones that don't cleanly plug into existing rules..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T04:18:46-07:00","id":1522048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1522004#post1522004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Losing my mind that we finally have a Storyteller's Guide, and<i> it doesn't have any guidance for handling Merits in play.</i><br /> <br /> On my knees begging for someone, anyone, to descend from their lofty eminence and explain the nuances of Influence and Resources and Backing and all the ones that don't cleanly plug into existing rules...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I understand what you mean. The main problem with those social merits is that there can be some overlap between them. I don't have any specific solutions for you, in my case I just talk it with the player to establish their limits and make them as clear and concise as possible. In any case, I look at it this way, having money or resources opens lots of doors, but it's useless if you don't know how to properly use it, it's a support tool for the skills where money or resources could play an important role; Backing is more simple, define who or what exactly is backing the player, what can they do, and what are they willing to do for the player; Influence is the most nebulous, that's why it's very important for the player to tell me how and why do they have that influence, also it's not mind control, like resources it's a tool to support skills if it's relevant, with an emphasis on social skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 09-04-2023, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T05:27:08-07:00","id":1522052,"title":"","content":"Along these lines, I would've also liked some solutions for when there's too many Exalts (or comparably powerful enemies) in one place for the combat system to handle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T05:05:38-07:00","id":1522508,"title":"","content":"I'm still reading the book and am working on a Youtube video about it (I like the book overall), but I'm waiting for the post-errata version before I finish it.<br /> <br /> I haven't read the essays on slavery and orientalism in great depth yet, but I want to point out that there are valid reasons to include it beyond the player experience. Exalted is a gameline that people either love or hate. It's hard to find nuanced takes on it. It's also been criticized for hypersexualization, orientalism, and a history of generally bad takes over the decades. Those who are on the hate-side of the Exalted-take polarity have concrete things to point at and say &quot;game bad!&quot; Including these kinds of essays help to defend the game against those criticisms, present a solid stance, and shift the game towards a better place in the larger RPG space.<br /> <br /> It's impossible to control how players approach things at their tables, and it's not a publisher's place to police what people do in their own homes, but taking larger stances helps the publisher distance themselves from certain problematic takes should those takes be public. You don't want to be the &quot;orientalist game&quot; or the &quot;slaver game,&quot; especially not after you were publically called the &quot;rape game&quot; in late 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T11:19:22-07:00","id":1522521,"title":"","content":"Arguably the slavery essay I think is generally better done, which is a bit why the Orientalism one gets a lot more focus by critics. And I agree, it is something I Think needed addressing or at least acknowledging, but it again, didn't give a lot ot do about it once acknoweldged which is disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T13:08:14-07:00","id":1522532,"title":"","content":"So as far as getting something more actionable from the Martial Arts part of the Orientalism section- I didn't generally go for the urban fantasy style secret martial arts world with my games and characters so that's not something that really needs fixing, but something I'm going to try and do more is to try and start more conversations about mentorship, training methods and fighting techniques with characters who favour other combat abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-13-2023, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T21:43:33-07:00","id":1522656,"title":"","content":"I find it kinda sad that while Exalted apologizes for using asian cultures as an influence, products like Obojima and Ryoko's Guide to the Yokai Realms are having so much fun offering exciting settings and character options clearly based on asian cultures.<br /> <br /> Exalted is soooo dead.... I mean, sure there are still folks that play it. But it is now so irrelevant as a playing option. I hope OP finally realizes that Ex3 is a baby that was born dead TEN YEARS AGO. Can we bury the poor thing and get a new edition? One that does not need 25 years to release the core books if possible. Oh, and Essence does not count, nobody is playing that thing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T23:23:28-07:00","id":1522658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1522656#post1522656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it kinda sad that while Exalted apologizes for using asian cultures as an influence, products like Obojima and Ryoko's Guide to the Yokai Realms are having so much fun offering exciting settings and character options clearly based on asian cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of a bit on maybe how the Orientalism essay doesn't really succeed, but pointing out the line has had Orientalist takes on foreign cultures is not apology for using Asian cultures for its influences and it is not a game that will avoid using othe rparts of the world besides Europe. It is different from thsoe games you note as ithey are trying to replicate specifically Japanese cultural concepts, in a Japanese context, in a way that is accessable to English audiences htat doesn't treat it as exotic, foreign, or fetishized. Exalted, by contrast, often engaged in a lot of the stuff that is as time has gone on not accepted takes on how to present Asian cultures by Western audiences. It's better than Kindred of the East, but not those properties.<br /> <br /> Drawing on Asian cultures is not, in itself, Orientalist. Drawing on them with an idea that it's an exotic Other to contrast with the &quot;normal&quot; West is. Exalted is guilty of the latter more than the former. The issue I have with the essay in CoL is it doesn't address what to do about it well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1522656#post1522656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted is soooo dead.... I mean, sure there are still folks that play it. But it is now so irrelevant as a playing option. I hope OP finally realizes that Ex3 is a baby that was born dead TEN YEARS AGO. Can we bury the poor thing and get a new edition? One that does not need 25 years to release the core books if possible. Oh, and Essence does not count, nobody is playing that thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see what this adds. You yourself say folks play it. It is often one of the fastest selling things on DriveThruRPG. This book itself is Gold on the site. Essence is Platinum. Exalted crowdfunding campaigns are consistently often Onyx Path's most suecessful. Even the least-bought-into one, <i>Exigents</i>, does better than other OPP books combined. Others bring in several hundred thousand dollars per campaign, with thousands of backers each.<br /> <br /> What matters in the end is sales and players. Exalted has both. And a new edition, even if it started today, would not be in anyone's hands any sooner than Alchemicals is going to be, because mechanics isn't all that make a book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T03:51:06-07:00","id":1522665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1521527#post1521527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the problem is also that charm empowered brawl particularly for Solar Exalted is a little too good in an end the fight by throwing a single punch kind of way and well, that\u2019s similar to how some people perceive the East vs. West divide where Asia has a lot of style and pageantry that\u2019s no match for brutal efficiency.<br /> <br /> There's something extremely macho about being <b>so strong</b> that it doesn't matter if the other person is more skilled than you and as I say this I realise that I'm struggling to think of a brawler (or hero stylist) among the named characters of 3 editions who was actually coded as Asian. I think possibly White Bone Sinner? Maybe!?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pleased to report that the answer is Tepet Yasal. He's an instructor at the House of Bells who fights the occasional exhibition match in pursuit of greater frame and recognition in the comic from Scroll of the Monk they're talking about the events of the Udon Comic series in which Peleps Taguro using Safety Among Enemies to redirect Demetheus' attack towards Kidale, killing the Eclipse caste and effectively breaking the Dawn Caste for the remainder of 2nd edition until he eventually ran into Lady Gaga in Hell.<br /> <br /> Yes, 2nd edition was this self-referential. <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/lyrl3Q2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T10:56:33-07:00","id":1522752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1522658#post1522658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see what this adds. You yourself say folks play it. It is often one of the fastest selling things on DriveThruRPG. This book itself is Gold on the site. Essence is Platinum. Exalted crowdfunding campaigns are consistently often Onyx Path's most suecessful. Even the least-bought-into one, <i>Exigents</i>, does better than other OPP books combined. Others brin<br /> <br /> What matters in the end is sales and players. Exalted has both. And a new edition, even if it started today, would not be in anyone's hands any sooner than Alchemicals is going to be, because mechanics isn't all that make a book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about sales being the only thing that matters. The last exalted products I paid for, I bought only as collection items, and I don't think I'm the only one possessed by that kind of old fan inertia. <br /> <br /> I keep backing the KSs but I've decided not to get the physical hardcovers anymore. They are very expensive, and are full of unusable rules I truly have no time to read anymore. I tried starting a Ex3 game a little more than a year ago, and my players, all experienced with TTRPGs, hated it, none of them had time to read so many charms or get involved with the more complex systems. And while there surely are ways to make things work, the people I've talked to, simply don't care about that. They have 5e and are happy with it.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact that the forum is so quiet since the great witch Hunt that decided the fan base. People getting banned all the time. So many great posters gave up on the game. If you post your homebrew today here, you're gonna get a couple of comments and that's it. No more discussions, no more guys sharing their talent. Oh, and maybe the discord is full of life or something I don't care. I don't even know which is the good one, but all the ones I've found are full of discussions about something else entirely. <br /> <br /> The fact is that things have changed, to a point in which this isn't exciting anymore. Books keep coming out at a glacial speed, but I don't think Exalted is getting any new audience anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T13:44:58-07:00","id":1522761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1522752#post1522752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about sales being the only thing that matters. The last exalted products I paid for, I bought only as collection items, and I don't think I'm the only one possessed by that kind of old fan inertia.<br /> <br /> I keep backing the KSs but I've decided not to get the physical hardcovers anymore. They are very expensive, and are full of unusable rules I truly have no time to read anymore. I tried starting a Ex3 game a little more than a year ago, and my players, all experienced with TTRPGs, hated it, none of them had time to read so many charms or get involved with the more complex systems. And while there surely are ways to make things work, the people I've talked to, simply don't care about that. They have 5e and are happy with it.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact that the forum is so quiet since the great witch Hunt that decided the fan base. People getting banned all the time. So many great posters gave up on the game. If you post your homebrew today here, you're gonna get a couple of comments and that's it. No more discussions, no more guys sharing their talent. Oh, and maybe the discord is full of life or something I don't care. I don't even know which is the good one, but all the ones I've found are full of discussions about something else entirely.<br /> <br /> The fact is that things have changed, to a point in which this isn't exciting anymore. Books keep coming out at a glacial speed, but I don't think Exalted is getting any new audience anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The forum is quiet because for over a year it was broken and unable to allow posts to be seen or interacted with. <br /> <br /> As for the rest your experience is your own, because I've had people start up and join in to play games and love it. <br /> <br /> But ultimately this comes down to you aren't being helpful or useful to the discussion, no one is holding you at gun point and your argument of &quot;Scrap the whole edition its taking too long just do a new one&quot; really misses the point that nothing would be solved by a new edition sure as fuck not that its taking a while to get the entire line out. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T09:30:56-07:00","id":1523080,"title":"","content":"I agree that its too little too late if you were one of the people who backed the 3rd edition kickstarter and successfully ran Exalted at any point in any previous edition but it's good that it's there and we'll hopefully feel the value of it in the coming years. It probably would've generated a lot more buzz with existing players had it come out before Exalted Essence and revealed the details on the Abyssals, Infernals, Getimian and Alchemicals. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1521527#post1521527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the problem is also that charm empowered brawl particularly for Solar Exalted is a little too good in an end the fight by throwing a single punch kind of way and well, that\u2019s similar to how some people perceive the East vs. West divide where Asia has a lot of style and pageantry that\u2019s no match for brutal efficiency.<br /> <br /> There's something extremely macho about being <b>so strong</b> that it doesn't matter if the other person is more skilled than you and as I say this I realise that I'm struggling to think of a brawler (or hero stylist) among the named characters of 3 editions who was actually coded as Asian. I think possibly White Bone Sinner? Maybe!?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>White Bone Sinner is a tricky one, his backstory with Panther would suggest a fellow brawler but he is also the original owner of Jiunan Nightwarden's grimscythe. I still like his depiction fighting Lilith on the cover of the 2e Storyteller's Guide which led to my partner calling him &quot;Goth Raiden&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T11:06:26-07:00","id":1523084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1523080#post1523080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that its too little too late if you were one of the people who backed the 3rd edition kickstarter and successfully ran Exalted at any point in any previous edition but it's good that it's there and we'll hopefully feel the value of it in the coming years. It probably would've generated a lot more buzz with existing players had it come out before Exalted Essence and revealed the details on the Abyssals, Infernals, Getimian and Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> White Bone Sinner is a tricky one, his backstory with Panther would suggest a fellow brawler but he is also the original owner of Jiunan Nightwarden's grimscythe. I still like his depiction fighting Lilith on the cover of the 2e Storyteller's Guide which led to my partner calling him &quot;Goth Raiden&quot;.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a grimcleaver. And apparently he wasn't very good with it, because Nightwarden managed to get it away from him and keep it away. And that's why WBS is also known as the Visitor in the Hall of Obsidian Mirrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T06:47:24-07:00","id":1523131,"title":"","content":"My mistake.<br /> <br /> I think it was more the loss of the ghost courtesan that got White Bone Sinner punished, but then again, the Walker in Darkness was portrayed as the kind of moron who would force a career brawler to use a grimcleaver and then torture him for losing it in a fight against a Solar. I cannot wait for better Deathlords. \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T07:48:52-07:00","id":1523134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520386-so-crucible-of-legends?p=1523131#post1523131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mistake.<br /> <br /> I think it was more the loss of the ghost courtesan that got White Bone Sinner punished, but then again, the Walker in Darkness was portrayed as the kind of moron who would force a career brawler to use a grimcleaver and then torture him for losing it in a fight against a Solar. I cannot wait for better Deathlords. \u200b<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he does use an axe himself, so...<br /> <br /> &quot;You lost your axe! Now how are people going to know that you're one of my deathknights? Axes are important!&quot;<br /> <br /> Six hours of lecturing about axes later, and White Bone Sinner gets thrown in the mirror room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T14:37:27-07:00","id":1524368,"title":"","content":"So should I hold of on buying Crucible of Legend until it's fully errata'd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","v